# SCOPE 4  |  Tier 2 saddle points: B3LYP-D3(BJ)/def2-TZVP, OptTS + FREQ
# State: V-TS2 first Al-O cleavage saddle  |  register row: V-TS2-T2-V06
# Start: TIER 1 accepted saddle optts3_bandB_ci (1 imaginary mode, -78.21 cm-1,
#      barrier +160.70 kJ/mol vs V-I1) - the one properly converged Tier 1 saddle.
# Why: it is the only barrier in the vanadium route that carries the mechanism, and
#      the A4 two-sided test FAILED at Tier 1 (the +0.01 nm displacement fell 107 kJ/mol
#      away from V-I1 instead of within 5). The Tier 2 job is the make-or-break test.
# Pre-registered decision rule (write it in the register BEFORE you look):
#    ACCEPT only if TERMINATED NORMALLY + converged OptTS + exactly 1 imaginary mode
#    AND the two +/-0.1 A mode-displacement OPT jobs (tools/gen_inputs.py --displace)
#    land within 5 kJ/mol of V-I2 and V-I1 respectively.
#    Anything else = 'not established at this level'; report the electronic barrier
#    bracket instead and say so in the limitations.
# Cost warning: OptTS with an exact initial Hessian (%geom Calc_Hess true) on 30
#      atoms is the most expensive job class in this package; treat 10-60 h per job
#      as the honest bracket and run them one at a time with a budget stop.
# Gate: TERMINATED NORMALLY + converged + exactly 1 imaginary mode animating the
#      reacting bond; then the A4 displacement test.

! B3LYP D3BJ def2-TZVP RIJCOSX def2/J TightSCF DefGrid3 OptTS Freq

%pal nprocs 4 end
%maxcore 3000

%scf
  MaxIter 300
end

%geom
  Calc_Hess true
  MaxIter 200
end

%freq
  Temp 298.15, 1003.15
end

* xyzfile 0 1 xyz/v-ts2.xyz
